{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The outdoor Gorilla tape feels like a natural next choice because I have used Gorilla tape before, and weather resistance adds a useful repair capability in a manageable two-pack.",
    "The waterproof crimp connector assortment builds on my previous terminal purchase and fits the electrical repair work I have bought supplies for."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Ten tubes of super glue exceed my current need; an adhesive can fit my repair interests without being a sensible purchase in that quantity.",
    "Magnetic hooks and pegboard accessories assume I have particular places to mount them, while O-ring lubricant assumes a maintenance task my clamp purchases do not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repair-supply purchases seem to have been taken as a broad interest in anything used around tools or maintenance, even when I have no matching task.",
    "My wiring purchases led to several related supplies, but I would choose the crimp assortment now rather than also buy solder connectors and separate tubing."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "A relevant supply is not always something I need now: foil tape relates to my recent duct clamps, but I would wait for a duct joint that needs sealing.",
    "Quantity and the specific repair matter to me. A small epoxy pack could be useful for a future bonding task, while a ten-pack of glue feels excessive right now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical repair interests but sometimes mistake a related supply for a current need."
}"}
